<title>USA: TABLE-Stanhome Q2 net income rises 6 percent.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Stanhome Q2 net income rises 6 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WESTFIELD, Mass. 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>STANHOME INC.</p>
<p>			     CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF INCOME</p>
<p>For the Second Quarter and First Six Months Ended June 30,</p>
<p>			 SECOND QUARTER	   FIRST SIX MONTHS</p>
<p>		  1997	1996  %Change    1997     1996 %Change</p>
<p>Net sales    $137,002  $130,823   5%   $239,062   $230,435  4%</p>
<p>Operating profit</p>
<p>		    19,898   19,264    3%    26,100     24,849  5%</p>
<p>Net income from continuing operations</p>
<p>		     9,759    9,320    5%    11,952     11,132  7%</p>
<p>Total net income/(loss)</p>
<p>		    11,569   10,951    6%    (20,190)     15,021</p>
<p>Earnings per share from Continuing operations</p>
<p>		     .55	.51    8%	 .67	  .61  10%</p>
<p>Total earnings per share</p>
<p>		     .65	.60    8%	 (1.13)     .82</p>
<p>Average shares fully diluted</p>
<p>		    17,781	18,219	 17,897	 18,300</p>
<p>			(In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
